00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.640 align:start position:0%
researchers at Northwestern University  have created a new material they call  hyper elastic bone it can be 3d printed  and used by surgeons to treat injuries  almost as soon as the printer finishes  once inserted this material acts as a  structural element and a scaffold for  bone regeneration in animal models it  encourages new bone cells to move in and  rebuild the injured area this means it  should help human patients regrowth  damaged or missing bone it's also  cost-effective and easy for surgeons to  customize and deploy hyperelastic bone  consists of hydroxyapatite the mineral  and bone suspended in an elastic organic  polymer it's flexible which makes it  easy to put in place but it's also  sturdy and should hold up until the real  thing grows in hyperelastic bone can be  printed at room temperature and handled  immediately it's flexible enough that  surgeons can cut it down to fit the  patient during the operation this  materials effectiveness and ease of use  set it head shoulders knees and toes  above the rest of the field  [Music]  you
 

